    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass (the project's test suite is the single `AcceptanceTest`, which now passes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `capacityWarning` flag that is `true` when an owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners (approaching the hard limit of 50), leaving the existing 50-owner hard rejection untouched.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Boolean capacityWarning` field (derived at response time, never persisted) with getter/setter, mirroring `bulkSignupWarning`.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` boolean property to the owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n\n3. **`rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerCapacityWarning.java`** (new) \u2014 counts owners in the owner's city and sets the flag when the count is in `[40, 49]`. It reuses `EnsureCityCapacity.CAPACITY` (50) so the warning band derives from the hard limit and stays in sync.\n\n4. **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** and **`.../owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `capacityWarning` step after the bulk-signup `warn` step in both pipelines. It runs after Save (create) and on read, counting all owners in the city including this one, so the flag is identical whether returned from the create response or a later GET \u2014 matching the pattern used by the other derived flags.\n\nThe test fills a fresh city to 40 owners, creates one more (making 41, within the 40\u201349 band), and asserts `capacityWarning` is `true` on the subsequent GET \u2014 which now holds.",
